The SYSGOTH bootloader!
yay a bootloader for GothRTOS heheh

SYSGOTH is the first-stage loader for GothRTOS. It waits for a
SparseKernel.img3 image, applies it to memory, and jumps to its entry point
so a board or machine can be (re)booted without reprogramming the whole device.

Targets
-------
- Pico / Pico 2 (`target_pico.c`, CMake build): receives SparseKernel.img3
  over the UART and boots it.
- AMD64 PC (`target_amd64.c`, `make sysgoth-amd64`): multiboot-bootable
  image (linked at 4 MiB) that shows status on VGA text mode and COM1 serial.
  It loads a SparseKernel.img3 from:
    - serial (COM1 at 115200), streamed by the host `sysgoth-flash` tool; or
    - a block device, by scanning for the SparseKernel magic in a
      filesystem-agnostic way. ATA PIO (HDD/SSD in IDE compatibility mode)
      and ATAPI (CD/DVD-ROM) are probed on the legacy IDE buses. Native USB
      mass storage and AHCI controllers need dedicated drivers and are not
      driven directly; media exposed through IDE compatibility is reachable.

Host tools
----------
- `sysgoth/main.cpp` (`sysgoth-flash`): streams a SparseKernel.img3 to a
  serial device for an embedded board running SYSGOTH.

Portable core
-------------
`sysgoth.c`/`sysgoth.h` implement the UART receive/apply protocol and share
the SparseKernel parser. Board/target files provide I/O, timing, writable
memory regions and the final jump.